When an organization identifies the needs and expectations of interested parties, it must determine:

* the interested parties that are relevant to its information‑security management system;  
* the relevant requirements of those interested parties;  
* which of those requirements will be addressed through the information‑security management system.  

[ S1 ]

Under Clause 5.2 an information security policy must contain the following elements:

- be appropriate to the purpose of the organization;  
- include information‑security objectives (or provide a framework for setting them);  
- include a commitment to satisfy applicable information‑security requirements;  
- include a commitment to continual improvement of the information‑security management system;  
- be available as documented information;  
- be communicated within the organization;  
- be available to interested parties, as appropriate.  

[ S1 ]

Clause 7.2 requires the organization to:

* determine the necessary competence of the person(s) doing work under its control that affects its information‑security performance;  
* ensure that these persons are competent on the basis of appropriate education, training, or experience;  
* where applicable, take actions to acquire the necessary competence and evaluate the effectiveness of those actions;  
* retain appropriate documented information as evidence of competence.  

[S1]

Under Clause 7.5.3 the organization must address the following activities when controlling documented information:  

- **Distribution, access, retrieval and use** of the documents;  
- **Storage and preservation**, including ensuring legibility;  
- **Control of changes** (e.g., version control); and  
- **Retention and disposition** of the documents.  

[ S1 ] [ S2 ]

Clause 9.1 requires an organization to determine:

a) **What needs to be monitored and measured** – including information‑security processes and controls;  
b) **The methods** for monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation that will produce valid, comparable and reproducible results;  
c) **When** the monitoring and measuring shall be performed;  
d) **Who** shall monitor and measure;  
e) **When** the results from monitoring and measurement shall be analysed and evaluated;  
f) **Who** shall analyse and evaluate these results.  

[ S1 ]
